Language level.  By default cc takes every addition to the MWC compiler's
K&R language: function prototypes and ANSI definitions, an automatic
structure initialized from a structure expression, an automatic array
sized by its initializer, switch on a long, & applied to an array (a
pointer to the array, at its first element), offsetof() as an integer
constant expression, // comments, and
declarations after statements and in a for.  -VKR, -VC89 and -VC99 select
a level; the last one given counts.  A feature above the level is an
error that names it, and the compile goes on as if it were allowed, so
one use gives one message.  Two features are refused the way the MWC
compiler refused them, without a message of their own, because K&R code
can contain the same text: under -VKR, f(T) with T a typedef name declares
a parameter named T, and under -VKR and -VC89, // is a division followed by
whatever comes next.  Under -VKR, & of an array is "lvalue required", the
MWC compiler's error, and offsetof() is not a constant expression, as
there.  K&R code compiles to the same object at every level.
The members an automatic aggregate's initializer leaves out are zero, as
a static's are, at every level.
-VC99 is a C99 subset: designated initializers, inline, variadic macros,
long long and the C99 library are not supported at any level.

Strict errors.  -VSTRICT makes every strict message an error: each
message the -VS options turn on (those printed "Strict:") counts as an
error, so the compile fails, and -VNOWARN does not hide it.  It also turns
on the level's own check, -VSBOOK ("construction not in Kernighan and
Ritchie") under -VKR and -VSVARG (an int argument in a variable argument
list) otherwise.  A feature above the level is an error with or without
-VSTRICT.  The two donor readings above, f(T) and //, stay as they are:
they are valid K&R.  -VSTRICT is variant bit 48, the first of a seventh
variant byte; a variant string is twelve hex digits as before unless a
bit of that byte is set, when it is fourteen, and a pass reads a string
of either length.

The driver names the i8086 and i386 model and floating-point variants --
-VSMALL, -VLARGE, -V8087, -VNDP, -VRAM, -VOMF, -V80186, -V80287, -VEMU87,
-VALIGN -- in the same table, because one driver serves several machines.
Of these only -VSMALL and -VLARGE mean anything here, as the model
selection described above; this build maps the rest onto a variant bit no
back end reads, so asking for one is accepted and ignored rather than
refused.

Files
/usr/bin/as      the assembler
/usr/bin/ld      the loader
/usr/lib/cc0     parser
/usr/lib/cc1     code generator
/usr/lib/cc2     optimizer and object writer
/usr/lib/crts0.o C runtime startoff
/usr/lib/libc.a  C library, linked unless -VLIB says otherwise
/usr/lib/libm.a  maths library, linked when -lm is given

